") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009074 \"A thymic medullary epithelial cell that expresses typical tuft cell markers instead of classical mTEC or cTEC markers. This population has a bulbous-like structure.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33597545\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009075 \"A thymic medullary epithelial cell that expresses muscle-specific biomarkers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32079746\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33597545\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009076 \"A thymic medullary epithelial cell that expresses neuroendocrine biomarkers.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:32094117\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7196501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009097 \"A skeletal muscle fiber found in an embryo. In mammalian embryos, skeletal muscle expresses myosin heavy chain-embryonic (MyHC-emb, encoded by the MYH3 gene), which regulates skeletal muscle development.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26180627\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7196501\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"http://orcid.org/0000-0003-2034-601X\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009098 \"A skeletal muscle fiber found at the fetal and neonatal stages. In mammalian fetuses and neonates, skeletal muscle expresses myosin heavy chain-neonatal (MyHC-neo, encoded by the MYH8 gene). This expression disappears shortly after birth and is replaced by expression of adult heavy chain myosins.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21435450\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22566825\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25998961\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28262465\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29752062\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34256989\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7655-4833\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0009102 \"A specialized, fibroblastic reticular cell of mesenchymal origin found in lymph nodes. In human, it expresses several markers common to myofibroblasts (desmin, vimentin, CD73, CD90, α-smooth muscle actin (αSMA)), and can be differentiated from endothelial cells by its lack of CD31 expression. These cells are critical for the overall organization and function of the lymph node. Lymph node fibroblastic reticular cells (FRCs) can be further classified based on their location, function, and unique marker expression.\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0010010 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0011003 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0046879))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011005 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0011006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0011006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061537))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011013 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000019 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0097722)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011016 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030317)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011024 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0002489 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0050777)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011105 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061527)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011106 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011104 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011109 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061585)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011110 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061538)))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:NV\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:20807514\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:21828096\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26053743\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34128468\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35067985\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011111 \"a specialized neuroendocrine cell that synthesizes and secretes GnRH decapeptide, a key regulator of reproductive function. It originates from the olfactory placode during embryonic development and migrates into the forebrain where it localises predominantly in the hypothalamus and in humans, in extrahypothalamic regions like the basal ganglia (Skrapits et al., 2021). This cell regulates reproduction by secreting GnRH into the pituitary portal vessels to induce the release of gonadotropins into the general circulation. It expresses receptor subunits required for AMPA, NMDA, and kainate receptor signaling and may use glutamate as a neurotransmitter in recurrent collateral innervation.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11138622\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:15514007\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0011114 \"A segmented neutrophilic cell of the bone marrow reserve pool that expresses CD11b (integrin alpha-M) and high levels of CD16 (low affinity immunoglobulin gamma Fc region receptor III) on its cell surface.\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_0011115 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000000 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030154)))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28428369\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29221729\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31156637\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0017009 \"A human dendritic cell that expresses the AXL and SIGLEC6 genes.\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0017009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_O43699))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0017009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P30530))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22527717\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:29714721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35237268\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:39358509\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0019032 \"A tuft cell that is part of the intestinal epithelium, characterized by a distinctive apical tuft and lateral cytospinules connecting to neighbouring cells. This cell senses luminal stimuli via taste receptors and succinate signalling, initiating type 2 immune responses through the secretion of interleukin-25 while modulating epithelial regeneration through prostaglandin synthesis. It expresses key molecular markers such as doublecortin-like kinase 1 (DCLK1) in mice (Hendel et al., 2022), and KIT proto-oncogene in humans (Huang et al., 2024). Developed from intestinal crypt stem cells, this cell requires transcription factor POU2F3 for its development.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31324739\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33707780\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34046914\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34497389\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020000 \"A mesenchymal stromal cell found in the gut during development, and interacts with lymphoid tissue inducer (LTi) cells to drive secondary lymphoid organ formation (Prados et al., 2021). It expresses LTβR, PDGFRα, and VCAM, and upon activation secretes chemokines(e.g. CXCL13) and cytokines to organise lymphoid tissue architecture and recruit immune cells in both mice and humans (Denton el al., 2019; Elmentaite et al., 2021). As a multipotent progenitor, an mLTo cell differentiates into adult stromal subsets, including fibroblastic reticular cells (FRCs) (Prados et al., 2021), and its descendants persist in the adult gut-associated lymphoid tissues to maintain immune homeostasis(Denton el al., 2019; Lütge et al., 2021).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11596046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28384468\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28949036\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35927027\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7127069\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020003 \"A projection neuron that has its soma located in the internal segment of the globus pallidus (GPi) of primates, in the central “core” region. It expresses parvalbumin, is primarily GABAergic, and projects to motor thalamic nuclei including the ventral anterior, ventrolateral, and ventromedial nuclei. In the rodent homolog (entopeduncular nucleus), the core subregion is characterized by concentrated parvalbumin-positive neurons targeting the ventral anterior-ventral lateral thalamic nucleus and receives inputs from the dorsolateral striatum innervated by sensorimotor cortices (Miyamoto & Fukuda, 2022). This neuron corresponds to the sensorimotor output population of the GPi, as demonstrated in human tissue and cross-species comparative studies (Wallace et al., 2017) and by classic tracing in primates (Parent & De Bellefeuille, 1982; Parent et al., 2001).\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020003 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020003 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013502))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:11596046\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28384468\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30755721\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33787995\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:7127069\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2022.03.16.484460\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020004 \"A projection neuron that has its soma located in the internal segment of the globus pallidus (GPi), in the peripheral 'shell' region. In mice and primates, it expresses somatostatin and shows dual expression of GABAergic and glutamatergic markers, enabling co-release of GABA and glutamate (Wallace et al., 2017). It projects primarily to the lateral habenula (Parent & De Bellefeuille, 1982; Wallace et al., 2017), forming the limbic/aversive output stream of the GPi.\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020004 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015665))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061527))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020006 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0014055))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020008 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0014055))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020008 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22726837\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25843402\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:25926446\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27194328\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37336974\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1101/2022.03.16.484460\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020009 \"A GABAergic neuron located in the external globus pallidus (GPe) that constitutes approximately two-thirds of all GPe neurons (Mallet et al., 2012, Dodson et al., 2015). Derived from the medial ganglionic eminence, this cell selectively expresses Nkx2-1, with roughly two-thirds co-expressing parvalbumin (PV) and one-third lacking it in mice (Mallet et al., 2012; Dodson et al., 2015).\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020009 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000011241))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020010 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:40993240\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020012 \"A fibroblast that is part of the hair follicle isthmus (mid-hair shaft). In humans, this cell expresses CRABP1/COCH/RSPO4 and tendon-associated genes (MKX, TNMD).\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31857493\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35069694\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020013 \"A fibroblast forming the connective tissue sheath that encloses the hair follicle epithelium from the level of the bulge downward to the hair bulb. This cell expresses characteristic markers, including DPEP1 in humans and COL11A1 and ACTA2 (alpha-smooth muscle actin) in mice and humans. Dermal sheath fibroblast possesses contractile properties mediated by calcium-calmodulin-myosin light chain kinase signalling, generating centripetal force during hair follicle catagen that relocates the dermal papilla to the stem cell niche.\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0006936))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003675))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005694))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020013 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P16444))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020014 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001243))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33893305\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37468583\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020015 \"A transitional cell located in the renal collecting duct that co-expresses markers of both principal cell (PC) and intercalated cell (IC). This hybrid cell is enriched in Chronic Kidney Disease (CKD).\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020016 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001649))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020016 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0017145))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020016 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0051216))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000003264))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000007498))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020020 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0070278))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_0020020 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_1990079))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31871141\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36338137\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020021 \"A mesenchymal progenitor cell located in fibrocartilaginous tissues, along the fibrochondrocytic differentiation pathway that co-expresses both fibrochondrocyte markers (COL1A1, COL3A1) and mesenchymal stem cell markers (MCAM/CD146, MYLK) in humans. This cell serves as a progenitor for mature fibrochondrocytes and other meniscal cell types, with differentiation regulated by TGF-β signaling, focal adhesion, and extracellular matrix-receptor interaction pathways.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:26735013\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:28753612\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:31784286\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35830791\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37066415\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_0020027 \"An alpha retinal ganglion cell subtype in the mouse retina that responds selectively and transiently to increases in light intensity. It possesses the large soma and expansive dendritic field characteristic of alpha RGCs (Krieger et al., 2017). This cell exhibits a brief, fast-decaying burst of firing at the onset of light increments and contributes to motion detection for luminance increases, forming the ON-branch of the transient magnocellular-like pathway (Krieger et al., 2017; Hahn et al., 2023). Functionally, it corresponds to cluster G19 and aligns transcriptomically with cluster C41 (Krieger et al., 2017; Tran et al., 2019). It is orthologous to the primate ON Parasol RGC (Hahn et al., 2023). Molecularly, it expresses Spp1, Smi32, and Brn3b, but lacks Brn3a, Brn3c, and Calbindin (Krieger et al., 2017).\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000222 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0046717))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000223 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0001820))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000223 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0070483))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000308 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013031))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000347 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0019626))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000347 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0035377))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"doi:10.1038/s41385-022-00565-0\") rdfs:comment obo:CL_1000486 \"It has been noted in at least some mammalian species that the urothelial basal cell type is distinguished by expression of high levels of cytokeratin-5 (CK5), p63 and the signalling molecule Sonic hedgehog (Shh). Similar to intermediate cells, the urothelial basal cell type expresses CK17 but is negative for uroplakins (UPK) and CK20. Urothelial basal cells have also been noted to be smaller in diameter than urothelial intermediate cells.\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_1000488 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000069 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:UBERON_0002394) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0015106)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000488 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:GO_0015106 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:BFO_0000050 obo:GO_0032782))))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000742 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0006909))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000742 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0070252))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000850 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0003093))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1000850 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_1900133))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1001474 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_1001505 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0030103))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_1001509 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061537)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_2000096 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0070278))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_2000096 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q15063))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"GOC:CellBLAST\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30429548\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30498493\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34745147\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:35438172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_3000001 \"A tissue-resident macrophage that is part of the placenta. A Hofbauer cell expresses high levels of growth factors and metalloproteinases that support vasculogenesis, angiogenesis, branching morphogenesis and tissue remodeling. A Hofbauer cell has a fetal origin, is found in the villous stroma, chorion, and amnion, and is present throughout pregnancy.\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_3000002 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011103 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061533)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_3000003 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0011103 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0014055)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_3000004 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_2000032 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0050906)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023007 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P32648))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023010 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023010 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000005460))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30382198\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023011 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Lamp5.\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023011 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000032148)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023014 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023014 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P32648))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33186530\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023015 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses Gamma-synuclein.\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023015 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015325)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023015 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015325))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33186530\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/e4ddac12-f48f-4455-8e8d-c2a48a683437.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023016 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron derived from the CGE and that expresses the vasoactive intestinal polypeptide. Its soma is located in the forebrain.\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023016 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000017299)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023016 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000017299))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27477017\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33742131\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:37824655\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"https://cellxgene.cziscience.com/e/9c63201d-bfd9-41a8-bbbc-18d947556f3d.cxg/\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023017 \"A transcriptomically distinct GABAergic neuron located in the cerebral cortex that expresses somatostatin (sst) and derived from the MGE.\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023017 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023069 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000015665)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023018 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013502))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023019 \"A VIP GABAergic cortical interneuron that expresses cck. L5/6 cck cells have soma found mainly in L5 and L6 and have large axonal arborization.\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023019 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_4023071 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P32648)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023022 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023022 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9D387))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023023 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023023 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9D387))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023024 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023024 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_Q9D387))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023025 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023025 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:2147780\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:215920\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:23354054\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34727523\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36741471\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9004351\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Medium_spiny_neuron&oldid=1109726850\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023026 \"A GABAergic medium spiny neuron located in the striatum that gives rise to the direct basal ganglia pathway. It projects directly to the GPi and SNr, where it inhibits tonically active GABAergic output neurons to disinhibit thalamic and brainstem motor targets (Gerfen. 2023). In mice and humans, this cell selectively expresses the D1 dopamine receptor (DRD1), which couples to stimulatory G-proteins (Gs/Gαolf) to increase cAMP and activate PKA-dependent signaling cascades (Gerfen et al., 1990; Kebabian & Calne, 1979). Functionally, activation of this cell promotes selected motor actions by disinhibiting thalamic and midbrain motor centers (Mink, 1996; Cui et al., 2013).\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023026 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001175))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023027 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023027 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023028 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023028 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:27453468\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:34727523\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:36741471\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:9004351\") Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"WikipediaVersioned:Medium_spiny_neuron&oldid=1109726850\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023029 \"A GABAergic medium spiny neuron located in the striatum that gives rise to the indirect basal ganglia pathway. It projects to the GPe, where its axon typically ramifies in two regions but does not extend beyond this nucleus (Gerfen et al., 2022). It selectively expresses the D2 dopamine receptor (DRD2), which couples to inhibitory G-proteins (Gi/o) to decrease cAMP and suppress PKA-mediated signaling (Gerfen et al., 2022). Morphologically, this cell displays fewer and shorter dendrites than the MSN-D1 and receives fewer glutamatergic inputs, yet it exhibits significantly higher intrinsic excitability (Gertler et al., 2022). Functionally, activation of this cell suppresses competing or alternative motor actions by inhibiting GPe neurons, leading through STN and other GPe circuits to increased GPi/SNr output and stronger inhibition of thalamic and brainstem targets (Mink, 1996; Tecuapetla et al., 2016).\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023029 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000001177))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023030 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023030 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023031 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023031 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 obo:CL_4023069)\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023036 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000013502))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023039 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0001876) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061535)))\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30096314\") obo:CL_4023056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P11087))\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30096314\") obo:CL_4023056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P26618))\nSubClassOf(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:30096314\") obo:CL_4023056 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P51885))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023064 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33372656\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023065 \"A GABAergic cell located in the cerebral cortex that expresses meis2.\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023065 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_000010317))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023068 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000540 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0010225) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061535)))\n# Class: obo:CL_4023069 (medial ganglionic eminence derived GABAergic interneuron)\nAnnotationAssertion(obo:IAO_0000028 obo:CL_4023069 \"MGE gaba interneuron\")\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:12637172\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023069 \"A GABAergic interneuron that develops from the medial ganglionic eminence and has migrated to the cerebral cortex.\")\nAnnotationAssertion(terms:contributor obo:CL_4023069 <https://orcid.org/0000-0001-7258-9596>)\nAnnotationAssertion(rdfs:label obo:CL_4023069 \"medial ganglionic eminence derived GABAergic interneuron\")\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023069 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0000956) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002202 obo:UBERON_0004024) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023069 obo:CL_4023063)\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:33184512\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023071 \"A GABAergic cortical interneuron that expresses cck. L5/6 cck cells have soma found mainly in L5 and L6 and have large axonal arborization.\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023071 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023071 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P09240))\nAnnotationAssertion(Annotation(oboInOwl:hasDbXref \"PMID:22357664\") obo:IAO_0000115 obo:CL_4023075 \"A sst GABAergic cortical interneuron found in L6 that expresses tyrosine hydroxylase. L6 Th+ SST cells have mostly local axonal arborization within L6.\")\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023075 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023075 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P24529))\nSubClassOf(obo:CL_4023075 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002292 obo:PR_P60041))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023076 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0070007) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023086 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0070008) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023087 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0070009) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\nEquivalentClasses(obo:CL_4023088 ObjectIntersectionOf(obo:CL_0000099 ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0000053 obo:PATO_0070004) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002100 obo:UBERON_0001950) ObjectSomeValuesFrom(obo:RO_0002215 obo:GO_0061534)))\nEquivalentClas